  "criteria": [
    {"id":"AC1","text":"`pdd -V` behaves exactly like `pdd --version`: stdout contains only the installed package version and a newline; existing local diagnostics stay unchanged, with no interpreter or token read."},
    {"id":"AC2","text":"`pdd -VV` prints the installed package version, the interpreter's full reported build identifier and its exact supported interface, test and app-map format IDs, then exits with code 0."},
    {"id":"AC3","text":"When existing GitHub sign-in, interpreter access or usable build metadata is unavailable, `pdd -VV` prints the local version and \"PDD interpreter: unknown\", then exits with code 0 without asking for sign-in."},
    {"id":"AC4","text":"`pdd -VV` uses at most one metadata GET with a ten-second limit, sends no source, starts no model or prompt job and prints no credential, raw server message or control character."},
    {"id":"AC5","text":"Invalid version syntax exits with code 2 before token reads, network access or other command effects."}
  ],
